WIDENED CHECKS (gated tournaments, exact rationals):
- M2 Weyl-phase (circular), n=5, primitive 5-subsets of {1..16} = 4311 configs:
    realizes 10/12; FORBIDDEN exactly {(13,4,(1,2,2,2,3)), (15,4,(1,2,2,2,3))}.
    Same 2 forbidden under all-candidate-times on {1..12} (786 configs).
- M5 winding-parity, n=5, primitive 5-subsets of {1..18} = 8436 configs, 0 non-tourn:
    realizes 11/12; FORBIDDEN exactly {(15,4,(1,2,2,2,3))}.
    Realizes the SAME-score cousins (11,4) [2478x] and (13,4) [121x] AND the
    regular (15,5) [641x] -- forbids ONLY the max-Ham (H=15) non-regular member.
- M2 is NOT merely the circular tournament: pure circular phase placement realizes
    only 4/12 at n=5 (forbids 8), but LRC-driven M2 reaches 10/12 because the
    binding degeneracies ((x-y)tau* hits Z or 1/2; 5878 such pairs) override the
    circular rule via the speed tie-break -- yet the top 2 classes stay forbidden.

CROSS-METHOD INVARIANT (the headline):
    The class (H=15, #3cyc=4, score (1,2,2,2,3)) -- the UNIQUE maximum-Hamiltonian
    strongly-connected NON-regular tournament on 5 vertices -- is FORBIDDEN by FOUR
    independent character-spectral maps: M2, M3, M3b, M5. Free arc-flips reach it;
    loneliness-driven character signs never do (n=5, exhaustive over primitive
    speed families). This is the strongest forbidden-class signal of the session.

DEAD (always transitive, H=1 only): M1 (danger-weighted lead count over near band),
    M3c (Rademacher half-circle vote), M6 (c_14(v_i)v_j - c_14(v_j)v_i).
